# HTTP server — an M2 validation project (docs/10-roadmap.md, M2 gate: "a
# small HTTP client+server project passes validation").
#
# Serves two connections on the fixed port 8093: a real HTTP/1.1 response,
# one request each, then closes. The paired client is http_client.lagom.
# Networking fails as errors (13.1/S-10), so every operation rides `attempt`.
# These two files are skipped by the differential corpus sweep (they need a
# coordinated peer process); crates/lagom_driver/tests/net_validation.rs
# runs them on both backends and across backends.

attempt open listener at 8093 if it fails then
    say problem
otherwise
    make listener equal to result
    repeat 2 times
        attempt expect connection from listener if it fails then
            say problem
        otherwise
            make connection equal to result
            attempt take from connection if it fails then
                say problem
            otherwise
                make asked equal to result
            attempt put "HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\nContent-Length: 5\r\n\r\nhello" at connection if it fails then
                say problem
            otherwise
                make sent equal to result
            close connection
    close listener
    say "served 2 connections"
